Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 05:22:40 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fix(horse): v17 river probe is default off after the league
 measured it negative

The 2026-10-15 horse audit raised league_layer_negative_pooled for
v17_river_probe: -0.11 +/- 0.04 bb/100 pooled over the audit's 7-day
window (8 runs), -0.20 +/- 0.09 on 2026-10-16. Over the 14 runs since
2026-10-03 it is -0.10 +/- 0.05; over all 32 runs since 2026-09-15 it is
-0.02 +/- 0.03. It has never resolved positive, and the audit rule is that
a significant-negative layer is ablated before further tuning.

- HorseLogic: the probe is opt-in (opts.v17RiverProbe === true).
- League: v17_river_probe keeps its name and sign; arm A turns it on.
- Ledger: flag text records the default; receipt floor removed.
- Audit (20261016101800): zero fires is layer_default_off, a significant
  negative confirms the default, a significant positive says it earned
  its default back. Built on the installed bodies (md5 matched).
- Test: no option plays exactly like the layer off.

Production footprint was small: 1,764 fires on 2026-10-15 of 4.03M decisions.

